stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Placed : SqlOrderStore.Checkout commits<br/>(Status = 0)

    Placed --> Processing : staff, on /Admin/Orders
    Processing --> Sent : staff - optionally with a tracking number
    Sent --> Completed : staff

    Placed --> Cancelled : the buyer (receipt or order history),<br/>or staff
    Processing --> Cancelled : staff only

    Completed --> [*]
    Cancelled --> [*]

    note right of Placed
        dbo.Orders.Status, a TINYINT:
        0 Placed, 1 Processing, 2 Sent,
        3 Completed, 4 Cancelled.
        The buyer is emailed at every change,
        in the language the order was placed in
        (Data/OrderEmails.cs) and sees the
        status on the receipt and under
        Min konto.
    end note

    note right of Sent
        The wording follows the delivery:
        "Sent" for a shipped order,
        "Ready for pickup" for a pickup.
        Completed reads "Delivered" or
        "Picked up" the same way.
    end note

    note left of Processing
        Staff set the status from a list on
        /Admin/Orders (Admin and Employee),
        so they can also correct a mistake
        by setting an earlier one, and may
        cancel until the order has been sent.
        Every change is written to AuditLog.
    end note

    note left of Cancelled
        Cancelled is the highest number on
        purpose: "may still be cancelled" is
        the test Status <= latest (Placed for
        the buyer, Processing for staff), in
        the same UPDATE that cancels - a
        second click finds nothing to cancel.
        In that transaction the items go back:
        stock is added back, animals return
        from Sold to Available.
        Cancelled is final: UpdateStatus
        refuses to move a cancelled order.
    end note
